VERDICT: PASS -- `no mirror interface port1.0.10` removed the configured mirror from port1.0.11;
`show mirror` printed nothing afterwards, the mirror line was gone from the port's
running-config, and the FULL running-config diff against the pre-group baseline was empty.
PROVEN: removal, and the absence of any configuration residue. NOT MEASURED: that the destination
port resumes forwarding traffic -- port1.0.10 and port1.0.11 are empty SFP cages with no link
(I-9), and `show interface status` does not distinguish a mirror destination on this platform, so
"returns to normal switching" is proven as a configuration state only. If the real AWPTCM steps
require observed forwarding after removal, this is PARTIAL, not PASS. Graded against a
reconstruction of the case from its title, not AWPTCM's text (I-4). The drafted removal command
`no mirror interface` with no argument is INVALID on the x960 (`% Incomplete command.`); the verdict
is against the corrected form `no mirror interface <source-port>`, and the rejection of the drafted
form is recorded in STEP 1 as evidence of the drafting error, not as a product defect.
